"""The labelled set `sensitive_text` is measured on (G235): every value here is made up.

``POSITIVES``: ``(kind, body, harness)``. ``NEGATIVES``: ``(body, harness)``. A body is what a stored episode holds: turn
markers where a writer writes them, none where it does not (a note, a dictation). Written against the detector's
reasoning, so it is the floor of a measure, not the whole of one: `scripts/sensitive_census.py` reads a real bank (counts
only) and `api/tests/test_sensitive_text.py` also runs real code talk from this repository through it.

Vendor shapes are written split ("sk-" + "..."), the convention in this repo's tests: they are made up, and a whole one
in a commit trips GitHub's push protection."""

